Z||000003||Oreif||10-03-2001||08:32 AM||||IRM's scoop comes set up for an 84. When I bought mine (for $200) It required trimming for the decklid. There are lines marked on the inside that show you where to trim for the 85-88 notchback hump or the 86-88 fastback. IRM use to trim them for your particular style but now they don't. The good news is the price dropped from $240 to $200 when they stopped trimming them. Both the scoops need to be trimmed. But I think the Showcars part has the wide base. If you look at the pic at the very bottom it looks like it sticks out towards the passenger side. In the Pontiac Performance Plus magazine it shows a car with a similar scoop. I don't know anyone who has bought the Showcars scoop yet so it just may be the pic they used. If they have the wide base bottom, it would be nice for the V-8 folks or anyone using carbs that needs space for the airfilter assembly.<P>As for contacting IRM, Here are all the Phone Numbers they have listed on their receipt.<P>Order Desk: 1-800-367-8423 or 1-301-948-3301<BR>Fax: 1-301-774-6909<BR>Email: IRMFIERO@aol.com<P>(Note: the aol name needs to be in caps)<P>Last time I called them I was told they were only taking orders on Tuesday's and Thursday's. But that was a few years ago. I do know recently that some members were able to buy items from them.<P>Hope this helps.<P><BR>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||10-03-2001||11:10 AM||||i just got an egr tube from irm a week or so ago and asked about the scoops. they said the price had dropped a bit but the guy i talked to wasn't sure how much. you still have to catch that one particular lady to find out much.<P>so orief, are you saying with a showcars one i could put a wider air filter under it? i've been looking at the air filters pepboys has and they're about 6" wide at the bottom and with my irm one i can't go much past 5".<P>group purchase...think about it.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
